WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.530
Design the analytics for every trip in the city.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.880
The design round carries the most weight.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.440
It decides the level you are offered.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:13.240
You need three things: a framework, the building blocks, and correctness.

5
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.175
First: a framework for the 45 minutes.

6
00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:17.762
Ask for the requirements.

7
00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:19.038
Estimate the size.

8
00:00:19.058 --> 00:00:20.525
Draw the simple design.

9
00:00:20.545 --> 00:00:22.610
Then go deep on one part.

10
00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.960
Ask three things early.

11
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.535
Who uses it?

12
00:00:24.555 --> 00:00:25.185
How fresh?

13
00:00:25.205 --> 00:00:26.395
How big?

14
00:00:26.415 --> 00:00:27.933
Do not start with the tools.

15
00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:30.520
Start with what the users need.

16
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.480
Second: the same blocks, in every design.

17
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.617
Ingest the events.

18
00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:35.430
Store them raw.

19
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:36.355
Process them.

20
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:38.190
Then serve the result.

21
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.177
Pick the serving store by the read.

22
00:00:40.197 --> 00:00:43.615
A dashboard and a lookup need different stores.

23
00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:45.825
Third: what goes wrong at scale?

24
00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.012
Events come twice.

25
00:00:47.032 --> 00:00:48.200
Events come late.

26
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.760
And one day, you must replay a week.

27
00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:54.895
So give each event a unique key, and make the writes idempotent.

28
00:00:54.915 --> 00:00:55.920
And reconcile.

29
00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:59.195
Compare the counts with the source, every day.

30
00:00:59.215 --> 00:01:02.105
Last: what lifts a design to staff level?

31
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:06.580
Add three things: how you migrate, what it costs, and how it fails.

32
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.265
Quick recap of data system design.

33
00:01:09.285 --> 00:01:10.965
Requirements before tools.

34
00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:11.990
Four layers.

35
00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.700
And design for duplicates and late data.

36
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.820
Now start the first lesson below.
